
# Perspective Projection
## Overview

This experiment explores how 3D world coordinates
are transformed into 2D image coordinates using
the pinhole camera model.

## Concepts
- Camera Intrinsic Parameters
- Camera Extrinsic Parameters
- Rotation Matrix
- Translation Vector
- Perspective Projection

## Technologies
- Python
- NumPy
- Matplotlib

## Implementation
The implementation consists of three main steps:

1. Transform 3D world coordinates into camera coordinates.
2. Apply the camera intrinsic matrix.
3. Perform perspective division to obtain pixel coordinates.

## How to Run
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python perspective_projection.py
```

